BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Public Star Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T220000
UID:260514lKJq4UtxRESOKYyv5sSBJQ
DESCRIPTION:Public Star Parties are the heart of the Robert Ferguson Obser
 vatory—your monthly invitation to experience the wonder of the night sky
  like never before. Whether you’re a lifelong astronomy enthusiast or si
 mply curious about what lies beyond our planet\, these gatherings offer so
 mething magical for everyone.Each month includes a variety of engaging ast
 ronomy presentations led by our expert docents. You’ll hear fascinating 
 stories about the cosmos and the science behind some of the objects you’
 ll soon be observing. These talks set the stage for an unforgettable night
  under the stars.Step outside into the darkness of Sugarloaf Ridge State P
 ark\, where the skies open up in breathtaking clarity. You’ll have the c
 hance to explore the universe through three of RFO’s massive telescopes\
 , each powerful enough to reveal extraordinary detail: lunar craters\, pla
 nets\, star clusters\, glowing nebulae\, distant galaxies\, and more. In a
 ddition\, a field of smaller telescopes brought and operated by dedicated 
 volunteers\, creates a dynamic\, community-powered observing experience.Ev
 ery month offers a new selection of celestial treasures\, and our friendly
 \, knowledgeable docents are excited to guide you. They’ll help you navi
 gate the night sky\, answer questions\, and point out objects that many pe
 ople never get the chance to see.Come experience the excitement\, curiosit
 y\, and shared sense of discovery that make Public Star Parties such a che
 rished RFO tradition. Free for members—and unforgettable for everyone!
LOCATION:Robert Ferguson Observatory
URL:https://www.simpletix.com/e/public-star-parties-2026-tickets-240100
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 SRJC Shone Farm Fall Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T150000
UID:260930yoIyf3ZZd0qC6G4YHvyHpg
DESCRIPTION:SRJC Shone Farm welcomes the community to experience our outdo
 or learning laboratory and campus during harvest season. \n\nThis family-
 friendly event is open to the public and includes:\n\nAnimal meet and gree
 t Meet the cows\, goats\, and sheep who call Shone Farm their home.\n\nU-p
 ick pumpkins\, apples\, and sweet potatoes Experience the bounty of the s
 eason by picking your pumpkin from our multi-acre patch. Pumpkins range fr
 om small\, cute\, and petite to those humongous in size\, weighing nearly 
 100 lbs. Come pick apples from our orchard and sweet potatoes from the fi
 eld.\n\nVegetable and flower farm stand Shop freshly picked organic produc
 e & flower bouquets grown by SRJC students and farm interns from the Susta
 inable Agriculture program.\n\nRotten fruit slingshot For the young and yo
 ung-at-heart\, enjoy shooting rotten fruit with our giant slingshot.\n\nHa
 y Rides Enjoy Shone Farm and the Fall season by taking a hay ride around o
 ur garden and orchards.\n\nTractor Show and Tell and farm equipment displ
 ays It takes a lot of machines to grow a bountiful harvest and maintain th
 e farm. See and learn about the tractors and machinery vital to the agricu
 ltural industry.\n\nProfessional Fall Photography Station  Capture memori
 es of this year's Fall Festival for your holiday card by having your fam
 ily's picture taken\, complimentary\, by an SRJC Applied Photography stud
 ent.\n\nWine tasting \\(21 and older\\) Taste Shone Farm wine and learn ab
 out the SRJC Wine Studies program.\n\nFood court & more!\n\nSpecial thanks
  to our sponsors:\n\nPresenting Sponsor: American Ag Credit\n\nGold Sponso
 r: The Richard Kunde & Saralee McClelland Kunde Fund\n\nSilver Sponsors: B
 ottle Barn & Western Farm Center\n\nParking is free. This is a cashless ev
 ent. No dogs\, except assistance dogs\, are permitted.
LOCATION:Santa Rosa Junior College - Shone Farm
URL:https://shonefarm.santarosa.edu/shone-farm-fall-festival
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BEAT: Belew/Vai/Levin/Bozzio Performing the Music of KING CRIMSON
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T200000
UID:261009iff8R7BQlUWhkVITUP6qqQ
DESCRIPTION:Following more than 100 acclaimed performances across North an
 d South America\, Europe\, and Japan\, BEAT returns this fall for the last
  North American tour. Former King Crimson members Adrian Belew and Tony Le
 vin are joined by guitar virtuoso Steve Vai and legendary drummer Terry Bo
 zzio to perform the music of the three landmark 1980s King Crimson albums:
  Discipline\, Beat\, and Three of a Perfect Pair. Rather than attempting t
 o recreate the original recordings\, BEAT brings this extraordinary music 
 to life with the spirit\, precision\, and adventurousness that made it so 
 enduring. Whether you've lived with these albums for decades or are discov
 ering them for the first time\, this is the final opportunity to experienc
 e one of progressive music's most celebrated catalogs performed by four of
  the best musicians on the planet.
LOCATION:Blue Note Napa Summer Sessions
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/beat-belew-vai-levin-bo
 zzio-performing-the-music-of-king-crimson/19592807/2026-10-10T20
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
