BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Retos en las Montañas (Challenges in the Mountains)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T150000
UID:260917fTlnN6JkcECueaAriuR3xg
DESCRIPTION:Join Jack London Park Partners and Sonoma Ecology Center staff
  in a series of intermediate hikes\, guided in Spanish\, between Jack Lond
 on State Historic Park and Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. Each hike is a roun
 d trip\, returning to the starting point\, and will increase in length or 
 difficulty. Not appropriate for children under 12 years old.\n\n1.    
  Sat. Oct. 10 – Jack London's Ancient Redwood. 3.72 miles\, 620 ft. elev
 ation (meet at Jack London State Historic Park).\n\n2.     Sat. Oct. 1
 7 – Sugarloaf's waterfall loop. 2.39 miles\, 610 ft. elevation (meet at 
 Sugarloaf Ridge State Park).\n\n3.     Sat. Oct. 24 – Upper Fallen t
 o Camp Via to Fern Lake at Jack London. 5.72 miles\, 1\,150 ft. elevation 
 (meet at Jack London State Historic Park).\n\n4.     Sat. Nov. 7 – G
 unsight Rock at Sugarloaf/Hood Mountain Regional Park. 6.44 miles\, 2\,129
  ft. elevation (meet at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park).\n\n5.     Sun. No
 v. 15 – Sonoma Ridge in Sonoma Developmental Center/Jack London. 9.67 mi
 les\, 2\,126 ft. elevation (meet at the intersection of Arnold Dr. and Har
 ney Rd.\, inside the SDC).\n\n6.     Sat.  Nov. 21 – "The Big Loop"
  at Sugarloaf. 7.37 miles\, 1\,739 ft elevation (meet at Sugarloaf Ridge S
 tate Park).
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/reto2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Aspirations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T180000
UID:260916cHkuD0nLFEGjk85U9C1hkA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  9/15/26\n\nOCTOBER EXHIBIT: ASPI
 RATIONS\n\nEXHIBIT DATES – September 28 – October 25\, 2026\n\nRECEPTI
 ON: SATURDAY\, October 3\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Laura Roney and 
 Linda Loveland Reid and learn about their art and inspiration.  Be sure t
 o take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work
  by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma County arti
 st\, Laura Roney\, unveils Aspirations\, a new collection of paintings in 
 oil\, celebrating the unique differing goals people set during our lives\,
  challenging us to take bold steps forward.  Of universal inspiration\, A
 spiration and Awe splashes the Milky Way’s starry brilliance across the 
 heavens\, capturing our imagination and hope as worldly cares are left beh
 ind.  Moving from natural forces to human endeavor\, looking toward socia
 l change\, Aspiring to Vote\, the portrait of a hopeful suffragette\, evok
 es the dream for a better future.  A lifetime goal for many\, the maratho
 n\, Aspiring for 26.2\, captures the early morning excitement waiting for 
 start times.  “People doing ordinary things but dreaming larger for the
  future has been a great inspiration for this series.  I hope folks will 
 be inspired by the boldness of people’s dreams\,” commented Roney on h
 er inspiration for the work.\n\nArt has been a lifelong passion for Roney.
   Beginning her art studies at a young age\, whatever avenue she was purs
 uing in life\, she continued her artistic endeavors.  After a successful 
 career in microbiology and pharmaceutical research\, a family move to Nort
 hern California enabled Roney to focus on her art.  She received her MFA 
 from Academy of Art University\, San Francisco.\n\nMeet the artist: Roney 
 will host the Gallery on September 30 and October 1 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n
 The Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Linda Loveland Reid’s Intentio
 nal Chaos\, a collection of exciting mixed-media works that explode with e
 xcitement and energy. Random patterns\, amorphous shapes and dancing dribb
 les magically coalesce into bold statements.  Intriguing and compelling\,
  like interlocking gears\, in Patterns of Memory multiple patterns interlo
 ck on fields of gold and black.  “I love throwing ink\, paint and even 
 coffee onto a blank canvas and creating through instinct\, gesture and emo
 tion.  Distilling energy into smaller works brings new challenges and som
 e happy surprises\,” noted Reid on her creative process.\n\nMeet the art
 ist: Reid will host the Gallery on October 23 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n Also
  join us for ART NITE HEALDSBURG\, Thursday\, October 1\, 5 – 7 pm.  AR
 T NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community 
 event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating.
   ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, He
 aldsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.   
  www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly
  Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Emilia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T221500
UID:260915kEhEfRNSbEy_eMwhsVN6xQ
DESCRIPTION:Emilia by Morgan Lloyd Malcolm is a passionate\, feminist rei
 magining of the life of 17th-century poet and musician Emilia Bassano. The
  play\, performed by an all-female cast\, delves into her journey from a p
 rivileged childhood\, to becoming a trailblazing poet\, and a woman fighti
 ng for her say in a male-dominated world.
LOCATION:SRJC Burbank Auditorium
URL:https://srjc.universitytickets.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:See 'ART IN ACTION' at  T Barny's STUDIO TOURS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T170000
UID:260915NB8Zf-j7VUChuds8ClywKg
DESCRIPTION:Sculptor T Barny invites visitors into his Alexander Valley St
 udio.\n\nFor two weekends \, October 10–11 & 17–18\, 2026\, visitors c
 an explore Barny’s working studio\, see sculptures in progress and finis
 hed works\, and discover how a block of stone becomes sculpture.\n\nAt 11 
 AM and 3 PM each day\, Barny will lead a special Studio Tour & Demonstrati
 on\, sharing the tools and techniques behind his direct-carving process. V
 isitors can see how he carves and polishes stone\, learn about the tools o
 f the trade\, and even pick up a hammer and chisel and try carving marble 
 themselves.\n\nWith more than 45 years as a sculptor\, Barny has created o
 ver 1\,000 sculptures\, working with more than 200 types of stone from aro
 und the world.\n\nCome meet the artist\, explore the studio and See Art in
  Action.
LOCATION:T Barny Gallery & Sculpture Garden
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/see-art-in-action-at-t-
 barny-s-studio-tours/19907916/2026-10-10T10
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
