BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Opening to the Flow of Connection at the Heart of Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T150000
UID:260715V6me5fxYhE2hY5q83_gNxg
DESCRIPTION:with Margarita Loinaz\n\nBeyond the confines of the conceptual
  mind\, life unfolds in a continuous flow that is unobstructed\, pervasive
 \, fresh\, and constantly revealing. The discursive mind with its strong p
 references interrupts this flow and disconnects us from the Earth\, each o
 ther\, and the greater cosmos. Through meditations with movement\, stillne
 ss\, and inquiry\, we will explore ways to recognize non-conceptual awaren
 ess\, noticing the shifts in perception that allow the flow of connection 
 to re-establish itself.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/opening-to-the-flow-of
 -connection-at-the-heart-of-life-mz1d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Laguna Open House & California Native Plant Sale
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T130000
UID:260711pdG0wbBt40qQrAzKX4OAyA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a festive\, free autumn celebration at the Laguna 
 Environmental Center. Take a guided walk through our native plant demonstr
 ation garden at 11:00am or 12:00pm\, explore the beautiful grounds\, and v
 isit **Spirit of My Homeland\, a new exhibit in Heron Hall featuring the 
 work of artist Gloria Armstrong**. The exhibit celebrates cultural connect
 ion\, family\, and place through artwork rooted in lived experience and lo
 cal landscapes.\n\nAs part of the day’s festivities\, the **Milo Baker 
 Chapter of the California Native Plant Society** will host their annual na
 tive plant sale in our shared nursery. It’s the perfect time to add habi
 tat-friendly plants to your garden and learn more about California native 
 plants.\n\nAdditional c**ommunity partners and organizations** will be jo
 ining us with resources\, activities\, and opportunities to connect with l
 ocal conservation efforts. More details coming soon!\n\nWe’re proud to o
 ffer this event as a celebration of art\, nature\, and community. Thank yo
 u for joining us to explore the native landscape\, support local conservat
 ion\, and connect with the Laguna de Santa Rosa.
LOCATION:Laguna Environmental Center
URL:https://2026LagunaOpenHouse.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T143000
UID:260626cquzfCHin0mnT13EuoSCfw
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\n*White Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil*\n\nSu
 sanna’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nThai Green Curry & Coconut Soup\n\
 n*Bliss Snap Peas & Heirloom Radish*\n\nYoung Vines Pinot Noir\, 2021\n\nH
 eirloom Potato & Cherry Tomato ‘Croustade’\n\n*Smoked Bacon-Grain Must
 ard Dressing*\n\nSusanna’s Vineyard Pinot Noir\, 2022\n\nRoasted Syrian 
 Seven-Spiced Chicken Breast\n\n*Indonesian Corn Fritter\, Summer Vegetable
  Ragout\, Balado Sauce*\n\nRosé de Blancs Sparkling\, 2021\n\nChilled Van
 illa Burnt Basque Cheesecake\n\n*Raspberry-Rose Syrup\, Black Tea & Licori
 ce-Poached Cherries*\n\n*Brown Butter Nilla Cookie\, Candied Lime*\n\n**Es
 tate Ingredients:**\n\nBay Laurel\, Cherries\, Chives\, Edible Flowers\, L
 emons\, Olive Oil\, Peas\, Potatoes\, Radishes\, Raspberries\, Thyme\, Tom
 atoes\, Zucchini and more!\n\nMenu by Estate Chef David Frakes\n\nReservat
 ions are required. Maximum group size is six guests.
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate 
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Twist of Fate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T213000
UID:2605298RVM49P8K0ubQVv23wOklA
DESCRIPTION:Twist of Fate\n\nOctober 10\, 11 & 12\, 2026\n\nWeill Hall\, G
 reen Music Center\n\n**Francesco Lecce-Chong\,** conductor\n\n**Maxim Land
 o\,** piano\n\n**MATT BROWNE:** Divertimento for Orchestra (World Premiere
 ) **FRANZ LISZT:** Concerto No. 1 in E-Flat major for Piano and Orchestra\
 , S.124 **PYOTR ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY:** Symphony No. 4 in F minor\, Opus 36\
 n\nThe season’s opener begins with a fanfare of fate\, which marks a poi
 gnant full circle for Francesco Lecce-Chong. He returns to the first piece
  he led with the Symphony: Tchaikovsky’s tempestuous Symphony No. 4. Thi
 s high-octane program also features fiery virtuoso Maxim Lando in Liszt’
 s thrilling Piano Concerto No. 1 and a world premiere by Matt Browne\, a c
 elebrated alumnus of the First Symphony Project.\n\n**Programs\, dates\, a
 rtists\, and prices are subject to change without notice. Tickets are subj
 ect to availability.**\n\nPhoto by Chris McGuire
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/twist-of-fate/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
