UID:26093021Yo30q8H0ehS8rrHfaLow
DESCRIPTION:**2026 Children's Jamboree & Marketplace - Come Grow\, Learn\,
  Play\, and Shop with Us!**\n\nThis fun\, free event for children and adul
 ts is Sunday\, October 11 from 11 a.m. to 2 p.m. at Nokhnoma Teaching and 
 Demonstration Garden in Santa Rosa.\n\n**Activities for children** will in
 clude items they can make and take home such as corn husk dolls\, sun catc
 hers\, gratitude banners\, seed pots\, garden art rocks\, and more! ﻿ 
 ﻿\n\n**Marketplace** will feature an assortment of 4-inch and 1-gallon s
 ucculents\, succulent containers\, succulent topped pumpkins in assorted s
 izes\, small and medium wreaths crafted with flora\, cones and/or succulen
 ts\, oyster shell succulents and decoupage oyster shell ornaments\, beaded
  light catchers\, and gardening books. All proceeds benefit the UC Master 
 Gardener Program of Sonoma County. Cash\, checks and credit cards accepted
 .\n\n**Information tables** will be staffed with Sonoma County Master Gard
 ener volunteers who will share home gardening information\, answer your ho
 me gardening-related questions and provide information about our programs 
 and projects.\n\n**Partner organizations** on site will include the Girl S
 couts\, Sonoma County Bee Association\, Children's Museum of Sonoma County
 \, Master Food Preservers\, Zero Waste\, Sonoma County 4-H\, and others.\n
 \nRegister to attend: Go to https://tinyurl.com/5dk8nw7r or sonomamg.ucanr
 .edu/ Upcoming Events to complete your registration. After registering\, 
 you will receive a confirmation email containing information about attendi
 ng the event.\n\n**General information**\n\nADA-compliant porta potty on s
 ite.\n\nADA parking will be available.\n\nWater available for filling wate
 r bottles.\n\nWear comfortable\, closed-toe shoes suitable for walking on 
 unpaved\, uneven paths\n\nBring a hat if desired.\n\nNo animals allowed\, 
 except trained service dogs.\n\nFood and beverages will not be available\,
  bring your own snacks or picnic lunch.
LOCATION:Nokhnoma Teaching and Demonstration Garden
URL:https://tinyurl.com/5dk8nw7r
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
