BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Harvest Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T160000
UID:260822_0664bFp8kKldPhVuvLdLQ
DESCRIPTION:We've laughed\, sipped\, danced\, and celebrated together all 
 summer long. Now it's time to ring in the fall season. Join us for the gra
 nd finale of our Summer Sundays series as DeLoach Vineyards transforms int
 o a vibrant harvest celebration filled with live music by Clay Bell\, loca
 l artisans\, delicious food\, and the warmth of community. Set against the
  backdrop of our vineyards during one of the most exciting times of the ye
 ar\, the Fall Harvest Festival is a celebration of everything we love abou
 t harvest season.\n\nDesigned with the whole family in mind\, the festival
  offers something for every age. Relax with seasonal wines by the glass or
  bottle\, harvest-inspired slushies\, and local food while browsing artisa
 n vendors. Kids of all ages are invited to enjoy pumpkin painting\, bobbin
 g for apples\, face painting\, and classic lawn games. Add in live enterta
 inment\, exciting raffle prizes\, and the beauty of autumn in the Russian 
 River Valley\, and you have the perfect way to welcome the season together
 .\n\n$25 per person | $15 per person (member) Children under 7 are complim
 entary.\n\nTicket includes a complimentary welcome pour for guests 21+.\n\
 nLarge party tickets with savings can be purchased here: https://www.explo
 retock.com/deloachvineyards/event/619514/fall-harvest-festival-6-ticket-bu
 ndle\n\nMusic to be performed by Clay Bell {https://www.claybell.me/}
LOCATION:DeLoach Vineyards
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/159659/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bhakti Yoga Daytreat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T170000
UID:260820RKrwHeVyDkWaDs1jrcQCHg
DESCRIPTION:with Janet Stone\n\nIn a world of constant noise\, this day is
  an invitation to return to the wisdom beneath it—to pause\, listen deep
 ly\, and reconnect with the heart of who you are.\n\nThrough meditation\, 
 breath\, yoga\, chanting\, music\, storytelling\, contemplation\, time in 
 nature\, and rest\, we’ll nourish the nervous system while exploring the
  stories that shape our lives. Drawing from the wisdom of the purāṇas
  \\(sacred myths\\)\, we’ll gently inquire into the narratives we’ve 
 inherited\, the ones we’ve unconsciously repeated\, and the possibility 
 of living a story that is more awake\, courageous\, and true.\n\nBhakti—
 the yoga of the heart—reminds us that every emotion can become fuel for 
 transformation. Chanting is a love letter to life\, inviting us to offer o
 ur voices to something greater while awakening our innate capacity for lov
 e\, grace\, resilience\, and devotion.\n\nJoin Janet Stone for a day of pr
 actice\, reflection\, community\, and stillness as we step away from the n
 oise and back toward ourselves.\n\nThis program will include a non-heated\
 , vigorous yoga asana practice.  In addition to the vigorous yoga asana 
 practice mentioned above\, our day together will involve a long\, strenuo
 us hike that includes steep sections of both uphill and downhill. You mu
 st be in good physical shape and not require any mobility assistance or de
 vices\, other than a typical trekking pole or stick for this program.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/bhakti-yoga-daytreat-s
 t1d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rare Tomato Tasting & Watercolor Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T170000
UID:260819DnIy2-MTLk6bNuhOxuZlxw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a unique experience at Hope Acre farm\, offered on
 ce a month during the harvest season. Taste a selection of heirloom tomato
 es before learning to watercolor your favorites with local artist and wate
 rcolor teacher\, Hannah Day.\n\nHope Acre grows over 140 varieties of rare
  tomatoes\; with rare titles like “Indigo Blueberry” and “Rebel Star
  Fighter”\, your tasting will include a wide range of flavor profiles. Y
 ou will dine on tomatoes that look identical but taste opposite\, tomatoes
  named after beloved drag queens\, tomatoes smaller than marbles\, and oth
 ers larger than a softball. Your tomatoes will be served sun warm\, straig
 ht from the vine\, with local bread and cheese\, and presented with passio
 nate musing by farmer Jai\, whose knowledge is expansive and excitement is
  infectious.\n\nAfter your tasting\, you’ll spend time looking even clos
 er at your favorite selections of the farm’s yield. Seated in the farm
 ’s lush outdoor space\, instructor Hannah Day will walk you step by step
  through rendering your subjects with close observation\, foundational dra
 wing skills\, and a unique approach to watercolor technique. With a mix of
  demonstration and individual instruction\, artists of all experience leve
 ls can walk away with a meaningful creative experience.\n\nBYO wine or bev
 erage of choice ~ vegan cheese will be served along with dairy selections 
 ~ Please contact with other dietary concerns
LOCATION:Hope Acre Farm
URL:https://www.hannahdrawstrees.com/paint-and-taste-tomatoes
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
