UID:260819GZ_9qbaxNk2eagnwS2IuUQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a unique experience at Hope Acre farm\, offered on
 ce a month during the harvest season. Taste a selection of heirloom tomato
 es before learning to watercolor your favorites with local artist and wate
 rcolor teacher\, Hannah Day. Hope Acre grows over 140 varieties of rare to
 matoes\; with rare titles like "Indigo Blueberry" and "Rebel Star Fighter"
 \, your tasting will include a wide range of flavor profiles. You will din
 e on tomatoes that look identical but taste opposite\, tomatoes named afte
 r beloved drag queens\, tomatoes smaller than marbles\, and others larger 
 than a softball. Your tomatoes will be served sun warm\, straight from the
  vine\, with local bread and cheese\, and presented with passionate musing
  by farmer Jai\, whose knowledge is expansive and excitement is infectious
 . After your tasting\, you'll spend time looking even closer at your favor
 ite selections of the farm's yield. Seated in the farm's lush outdoor spac
 e\, instructor Hannah Day will walk you step by step through rendering you
 r subjects with close observation\, foundational drawing skills\, and a un
 ique approach to watercolor technique. With a mix of demonstration and ind
 ividual instruction\, artists of all experience levels can walk away with 
 a meaningful creative experience. BYO wine or beverage of choice - vegan c
 heese will be served along with dairy selections - Please contact with oth
 er dietary concerns
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/rare-tomato-tasting-watercolor-worksh
 op/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sundays in Sonoma at Viansa Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T000000
UID:260624X4jpIn8-hE-pqmMD4XEuEA
DESCRIPTION:Viansa Winery feels made for live music\, perched atop the Sum
 mit of Sonoma with sweeping vineyard views and Tuscan-inspired charm. This
  summer and fall\, acclaimed singer-songwriter Greg Lamboy brings his warm
 \, intimate sound to the hilltop terrace for select afternoon performances
  as part of Viansa's outdoor music series. An award-winning guitarist and 
 frontman of the Americana band Pacific Standard\, Lamboy is known for pitc
 h-perfect melodies and deeply personal lyrics. His relaxed\, soulful style
  pairs effortlessly with Viansa's panoramic setting\, estate wines\, and l
 aid-back elegance. Settle in with a tasting\, take in the views\, and enjo
 y an afternoon where strong vocals\, masterful guitar\, and unforgettable 
 songs rise above the everyday. Performance Dates: June 14\, June 21\, July
  12\, July 19\, July 26\, October 4\, and October 18 from 12 pm -3 pm.
LOCATION:Viansa Winery
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/sundays-in-sonoma-at-viansa-winery/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
