DESCRIPTION:Explore the landscape\, history\, and cultural significance of
  Tolay Lake near the southern foot of Sonoma Mountain. On Indigenous Peopl
 es Day\, join Sonoma Mountain Preservation for a hike focused on Indigenou
 s connections to this special place extending back thousands of years\, an
 d the continuing relationship between people and the land.\n\nSMP board me
 mbers Nancy Kirwan and Mark Hannon will lead the hike\, with planned parti
 cipation from the Federated Indians of Graton Rancheria and Sonoma State U
 niversity. Along the way\, we will pause to discuss and explore Tolay’s 
 connections to the broader Sonoma Mountain landscape.
