BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Country
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T190000
UID:260807U22WxL1duUaUoE8WvmzABQ
DESCRIPTION:**“Haunted Wine Country” returns to the Sebastiani for one
  ghostly night**. **Friday October 16th\, 2026 @ 7:00PM**\n\nFor more than
  a century\, the natural beauty of Northern California's wine country has 
 drawn people from across the globe. But among the hardworking residents wh
 o made their homes there more than a century ago lurked a seedy and danger
 ous element: gamblers\, thieves\, prostitutes\, murderers -- even pirates.
  Death or ruin traveled with them. And long after committing their untowar
 d deeds\, the spirits of many remain there roaming the hillsides\, frighte
 ning current residents and turning this otherwise serene area into Haunted
  Wine Country. Paranormal experts\, authors\, historians\, ghost hunters a
 nd gifted psychics recount the area's ghostly tales and describe their per
 sonal experiences.
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theatre
URL:https://www.sebastianitheatre.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T143000
UID:260626xHraupTgt0eIlcmiH2qyuA
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\n*White Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil*\n\nSu
