BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Estate Luncheon Featuring The Big Green Egg | Gather for Thanksgiv
 ing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150700
UID:2608208XXzSJaN1k25oDdSGgEbzQ
DESCRIPTION:Join St. Supéry for this season’s estate luncheon series fe
 aturing The Big Green Egg. Enjoy wine and food pairings prepared entirely 
 on the Big Green Egg kamado grill by our Estate Chef Vince Sanchez. Guests
  will learn how to pair wine with food in a 3-hour\, immersive experience.
  This collaborative lunch demonstrates the ease and versatility of the Big
  Green EGG complete outdoor cooking system. Each themed lunch focuses on h
 ow to use a wide range of cooking options\, from High-Temp Grilling\, Low 
 & Slow Smoker to Outdoor Oven\, while the St. Supéry team will discuss ho
 w to pair wines with seasonal produce and fruit as well as a variety of me
 at and fish depending on the lunch theme. This lunch shows you how to perf
 ectly pair wine and food no matter the season. Event includes reception\, 
 grilling demonstration\, wine pairings and lunch. Wine Club members enjoy 
 30% savings. $150 per person\, tax and service fee. Space is limited. Rese
 rve your seat on Tock. October 16 & 17\, 2026 – BBQ Smoked Meats Gather 
 for a pre-holiday season luncheon to learn tips and tricks when preparing 
 grilled turkey as well as insightful twists on sides to delight your famil
 y and friends. Raise a glass to harvest with the latest wine releases and 
 plan your holiday celebrations. Wine Club Members enjoy 30% savings\, for 
 parties up to 6. Taxes and a 20% Service Fee is added to this event fee at
  time of purchase. Reserve on Tock. Seating is limited.
LOCATION:St. Supery Estate
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/2327366594464646/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop: Pulp Painting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T160000
UID:260819keWr_o_bTkSbfsHjgehR4w
DESCRIPTION:Using finely-beaten\, pigmented paper pulp\, students will mak
 e imagery on freshly pulled sheets of handmade paper. Participants will le
 arn introductory handmade paper techniques such as Western sheet formation
 \, as well as surface design methods of pulp painting\, stenciling\, and i
 nclusions. When dried\, pulp paintings are a part of the paper itself!Elem
 ents such as photos\, hair\, leaves\, and newspaper clippings can be embed
 ded into newly made sheets of paper or by using methyl cellulose as an adh
 esive. Please be aware that papermaking is a wet activity - wear clothing 
 and shoes that can get wet. Class involves some physical activity\, includ
 ing standing and arm movements. All supplies are provided through the mate
 rials fee. La maestra habla español.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/workshop-pulp-painting/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
