UID:261003iXp9yTBjxUylbi2m7XGyFA
DESCRIPTION:“There is no blues band performing today as different as How
 ellDevine—nor as delightful.”\n\n~ Lee Hildebrand\, Living Blues Magaz
 ine/SF Chronicle\n\n"...just when it seems like all the \\[blues\\] permut
 ations have been heard and it might be time to hang it up\, a trio like Ho
 wellDevine shows that in reality the road is endless..."         ~ Bi
 ll Bentley\, Author\; Concord Music Group\n\n"HowellDevine plays The Music
  with the original feel\, intent and spirit\, and you can tell they love t
 he music while delivering some real blues in their own way. The singing an
 d playing is never strained and they play with easy confidence...they don
 ’t have to prove anything.  There’s tasty slide\, harp and rhythm wit
 h relaxed vocals that all blend together for a wonderfully satisfying expe
 rience...it knocks me out to hear a group playing such good quality blues 
 today."  ~ Charlie Musselwhite\n\n"What a pleasure to find a young band t
 hat really gets the blues...Deep and true to the roots." ~ Bonnie Raitt\n\
 nTriple threat talent\, Joshua Howell \\(guitar\, harmonica\, vocals\\)\, 
 veteran upright bassist\, Joe Kyle Jr.\, and the dynamic J. Hansen on drum
 s mix rural blues with wildly syncopated rhythms to create a rollicking so
 und that stands in stark contrast to the typical blues heard these days. O
 riginally formed by Joshua Howell and drummer Pete Devine\, the band’s s
 ignature sound grew from their deeply shared rhythmic sensibility. The ban
 d was the first blues act signed by Chris Strachwitz to his legendary Arho
 olie Records label in over 27 years\, a testament to HowellDevine’s abil
 ity breathe life back into the early blues with their stamp of propulsive\
 , hypnotic rhythms.
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:https://ci.ovationtix.com/35892/performance/11867048
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
