SUMMARY:American Doctor documentary
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T203000
UID:261010frXTLkc2BUmoy9fCBpM97Q
DESCRIPTION:From Emmy® Award-winning filmmaker Poh Si Teng\, AMERICAN DOC
 TOR follows\n\nthree American physicians— Palestinian\, Jewish\, and Zor
 oastrian—united by a\n\nsingle oath to save lives. After volunteering in
  besieged hospitals in Gaza\, they\n\nreturn home determined to fight for 
 the patients and colleagues they left\n\nbehind\, taking their battle from
  the front lines of war to the halls of Congress.
LOCATION:Cameo Cinema
URL:https://www.cameocinema.com/movie/american-doctor-benefit-screening
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Joseph Hooker: Sonoma Valley's Soldier\, Gambler & Farmer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T203000
UID:261009CDtCSHA_jkqdnutma1ntpQ
DESCRIPTION:Joseph Hooker is remembered in history as a complex and highly
  controversial military figure. Understanding his past helps explain his f
 uture and his decisions. Before gaining national fame as the commander of 
 the Union's famous Army of the Potomac\, he faced both professional and pe
 rsonal struggles in Sonoma Valley\, many of which he caused himself. Durin
 g his time in Sonoma\, his well-known ego\, brashness\, and questionable d
 ealings led to a series of costly mistakes that would follow him into the 
 Civil War.\n\nJoin us for a fascinating presentation by author Travis P. W
 agner. He will share new information on "Fighting Joe" Hooker's turbulent 
 years in Sonoma Valley. His talk will explore the complex man behind the m
 yth. It will cover his time as a military officer\, a high-stakes gambler\
 , and a struggling frontier farmer\, before he achieved fame in the Civil 
 War.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center - Andrews Hall
URL:https://sonomavalleyhistory.org/event/joseph-hooker-sonoma-valleys-sol
 dier-gambler-farmer/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Healthy Hearty Meal Prep with Erin Shallat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T120000
UID:261005DMW4oR_z-EWevhygVFK1pg
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, October 5\, 2026 10:00 am to 12:00 pm\n\nWeekly on Mo
 ndays\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nCategory\n\nCulinary Art
 s\, Wellness\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\n
 Registration Cost:\n\n$25\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registrat
 ion Cost:\n\n$25\n\nAs the founder of Erin Shallat Catering in San Francis
 co\, Erin brings over two decades of experience in transforming nutrition 
 into an art form. Her unique approach intertwines advanced studies in nutr
 ition with a deep passion for the culinary arts. Erin’s goal is to make 
 meal prep approachable and not intimidating for everyone\, encouraging stu
 dents to gain confidence in the kitchen. She believes in working with seas
 onal produce and what’s available\, helping students learn to create hea
 lth-conscious yet tantalizing menus that embrace both flavor and wellness.
  Introducing our Fall/Winter Cooking Series—designed for both returning 
 and new students. This six-week program runs Mondays and Wednesdays\, each
  with a unique focus to offer variety\, skill-building\, and fun throughou
 t the season.Every Monday\, students will dive into healthy\, hearty meal 
 prep sessions. Each class focuses on creating nutritious\, satisfying dish
 es that can be portioned out and taken home—perfect for fueling the week
  ahead. These hands-on sessions ensure participants leave with ready-to-ea
 t meals and new confidence in their culinary skills.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/healthy-hearty-meal-prep-wi
 th-erin-shallat/2026-10-05/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Isis Howard: Monarch Conservation & the Power of Community Science
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T203000
UID:261003gyIY03YclEmT_gWo1M6qXg
DESCRIPTION:**Monarch Conservation & the Power of Community Science**\n\nI
 sis Howard\, Conservation Biologist\, The Xerces Society for Invertebrate 
 Conservation\n\nWant to help the monarch butterfly? Join us and the Xerces
  Society for an inspiring science talk on the western monarch population. 
 Learn about these butterflies' incredible migration to our California coas
 tline\, their fragile ecology\, and the simple steps we can all take to he
 lp them recover. While actions are urgent\, the opportunities for impact a
 re great. You'll leave with fun facts\, local community connections\, and 
 a clear vision of your role in the monarch's comeback story.\n\nBased in S
 onoma County\, California\, Isis works to protect western monarch butterfl
 ies across their breeding\, migratory\, and overwintering ranges. She prov
 ides technical assistance and training to land managers and the public on 
 habitat restoration\, monitoring and data collection\, and pollinator cons
 ervation. She also manages community science programs\, including the West
 ern Monarch Count and Western Monarch Milkweed Mapper\, and coordinates th
 e International Monarch Monitoring Blitz with several national partners. I
 sis is an experienced outdoor educator and holds a bachelor of science deg
 ree in environmental management and protection from Cal Poly\, San Luis Ob
 ispo
LOCATION:First United Methodist Church
URL:https://www.madroneaudubon.org/speakers
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Aspirations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T180000
UID:260916XDsk8DrxNEydzkrkm6SLOg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  9/15/26\n\nOCTOBER EXHIBIT: ASPI
 RATIONS\n\nEXHIBIT DATES – September 28 – October 25\, 2026\n\nRECEPTI
 ON: SATURDAY\, October 3\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Laura Roney and 
 Linda Loveland Reid and learn about their art and inspiration.  Be sure t
 o take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work
  by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma County arti
 st\, Laura Roney\, unveils Aspirations\, a new collection of paintings in 
 oil\, celebrating the unique differing goals people set during our lives\,
  challenging us to take bold steps forward.  Of universal inspiration\, A
 spiration and Awe splashes the Milky Way’s starry brilliance across the 
 heavens\, capturing our imagination and hope as worldly cares are left beh
 ind.  Moving from natural forces to human endeavor\, looking toward socia
 l change\, Aspiring to Vote\, the portrait of a hopeful suffragette\, evok
 es the dream for a better future.  A lifetime goal for many\, the maratho
 n\, Aspiring for 26.2\, captures the early morning excitement waiting for 
 start times.  “People doing ordinary things but dreaming larger for the
  future has been a great inspiration for this series.  I hope folks will 
 be inspired by the boldness of people’s dreams\,” commented Roney on h
 er inspiration for the work.\n\nArt has been a lifelong passion for Roney.
   Beginning her art studies at a young age\, whatever avenue she was purs
 uing in life\, she continued her artistic endeavors.  After a successful 
 career in microbiology and pharmaceutical research\, a family move to Nort
 hern California enabled Roney to focus on her art.  She received her MFA 
 from Academy of Art University\, San Francisco.\n\nMeet the artist: Roney 
 will host the Gallery on September 30 and October 1 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n
 The Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Linda Loveland Reid’s Intentio
 nal Chaos\, a collection of exciting mixed-media works that explode with e
 xcitement and energy. Random patterns\, amorphous shapes and dancing dribb
 les magically coalesce into bold statements.  Intriguing and compelling\,
  like interlocking gears\, in Patterns of Memory multiple patterns interlo
 ck on fields of gold and black.  “I love throwing ink\, paint and even 
 coffee onto a blank canvas and creating through instinct\, gesture and emo
 tion.  Distilling energy into smaller works brings new challenges and som
 e happy surprises\,” noted Reid on her creative process.\n\nMeet the art
 ist: Reid will host the Gallery on October 23 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n Also
  join us for ART NITE HEALDSBURG\, Thursday\, October 1\, 5 – 7 pm.  AR
 T NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community 
 event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating.
   ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, He
 aldsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.   
  www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly
  Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
