BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sandra von Arb\, co-author of Dragonflies (Anisoptera) of Californ
 ia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T210000
UID:261005WpXDX_YlWE6alMyH9GqNOQ
DESCRIPTION:Learn about colorful and interesting dragonflies and their uni
 que biology with field biologist Sandra von Arb\, co-author of Dragonflies
  \\(Anisoptera\\) of California with Kathy Biggs. Sandra will share her kn
 owledge of the 47 species that occur here\, how to identify them\, what th
 e dragonflies need for survival\, where to find them\, and their migratory
  habits.\n\nSandra von Arb has been a professional wildlife biologist for 
 30 years\, focusing on sensitive and endangered species in northern Califo
 rnia\, southern Oregon\, and northern Illinois. She is a co-founder of Bio
 diversity Education and Research Foundation\, whose mission is to foster e
 cological stewardship through science and education.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Art and Garden Center
URL:http://www.chapters.cnps.org/milobaker/events-and-activities/general-m
 eeting-speaker-series/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
