BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sing Napa Valley presents "American Songbook Singer Showcase"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T170000
UID:261008KuTDL1hS20uWNkAmvTe7nw
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate America’s musical heritage with Sing Napa Valley a
 t the American Songbook Singer Showcase. Presented in honor of the United 
 States’ 250th anniversary\, this lively afternoon concert travels from t
 he 1920s through the early 1960s with jazz standards\, Broadway favorites\
 , and memorable songs from film. Two concerts: Saturday\, October 24 & Sun
 day\, October 25 at 3pm.\n\nWhether these classics are lifelong favorites 
 or brand-new discoveries\, American Songbook Singer Showcase promises an u
 plifting celebration of music’s power to bridge generations and bring pe
 ople together.\n\nEnjoy timeless music by George and Ira Gershwin\, Cole P
 orter\, Hoagy Carmichael\, and Irving Berlin\, including favorites such as
  “Mr. Sandman\,” “Honeysuckle Rose\,” “Night and Day\,” and 
 “Dream a Little Dream of Me.” Sing Napa Valley choir members and speci
 al guests will take the spotlight in solos\, duets\, trios\, and small ens
 embles\, joined by collaborative pianist Anthony Mayor. Bring family and f
 riends for an uplifting celebration of music that connects generations.
LOCATION:American Legion Hall
URL:http://www.singnapavalley.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Whole New World - The Disney Songs of Alan Menken
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T153000
UID:261007kDKag_iuv06DGuC-ifXO-A
DESCRIPTION:Discover the unforgettable songs of Alan Menken\, the composer
  whose music has inspired generations to dream bigger\, love deeper\, and 
 find the courage to become who they are. This enchanting cabaret journeys 
 through the remarkable career of the Academy Award-winning composer\, feat
 uring fresh arrangements of beloved favorites from “The Little Mermaid\,
 ” “Beauty and the Beast\,” “Aladdin\,” “Little Shop of Horrors
 \,” “Newsies\,” “The Hunchback of Notre Dame\,” and more.\n\nWov
 en together through stories of imagination\, hope\, and transformation\, t
 hese timeless songs celebrate the extraordinary collaborations that have s
 haped some of the most cherished works of musical theatre and film. Perfor
 med by world-class artists\, this uplifting celebration promises an unforg
 ettable afternoon filled with heart\, humor\, and a little bit of magic.
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/a-whole-new-world-2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
