BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rocky Horror Picture Show With Full Shadow Cast and Costume Contes
 t
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T223000
UID:260906x1EWKiS4lEqIWevV4-bzQw
DESCRIPTION:Don’t dream it. Be it!\n\nSonoma Valley Pride is bringing T
 he Rocky Horror Picture Show back to the historic Sebastiani Theatre for 
 our second annual screening and costume contest — and this year\, we
 ’re taking it to a whole new level.\n\nFor the first time\, Rocky comes 
 to life with a full shadow cast performed by San Francisco’s Bawdy Cast
 e!\n\nWatch the cult classic on the big screen while a live cast performs 
 along with the film right in front of you. Expect outrageous audience part
 icipation\, props for throwing\, ridiculous costumes\, plenty of callback
 s\, and a costume contest celebrating your very best Rocky Horror looks.\n
 \nWhether you’ve been doing the Time Warp for decades or this is your fi
 rst trip to Frankenstein Place\, come ready for a night of camp\, chaos\, 
 community\, and absolute fun.\n\nAll proceeds benefit Sonoma Valley Pride!
  \n\nSchedule\n\n6:30 PM — Doors Open\n\nCome early\, grab your seat\, s
 how off your look\, and get ready for the night.\n\n7:00 PM — Pre-Show &
  Costume Contest\n\nWe’ll kick things off with our costume contest\, pre
 -show festivities\, and all the preparation you need before the madness be
 gins.\n\n7:40 PM — The Rocky Horror Picture Show \\+ Live Shadow Cast\n\
 nThe film begins with SF’s Bawdy Caste performing live alongside the mo
 vie.\n\nGuests are highly encouraged to come dressed as their favorite Roc
 ky Horror character — or simply embrace the spirit of the night and wea
 r something fabulous\, outrageous\, strange\, glamorous\, or completely ov
 er the top.\n\nPrizes will be awarded to some of our favorite looks of the
  evening.\n\nAnd yes — audience participation is strongly encouraged.\n
 \nRemembering a Legend\n\nThis year’s screening will be especially bitte
 rsweet following the passing of Tim Curry\, whose unforgettable portrayal
  of Dr. Frank-N-Furter helped make The Rocky Horror Picture Show the cul
 tural phenomenon it is today.\n\nFor generations\, Rocky Horror has permit
 ted people to be louder\, stranger\, freer\, more theatrical\, and more un
 apologetically themselves.\n\nThis October\, we’ll gather together to ce
 lebrate Tim Curry\, the character he made iconic\, and the enduring spirit
  of individuality\, freedom\, and queer joy that continues to make Rocky H
 orror so meaningful.\n\nSo grab your fishnets\, warm up your Time Warp\, g
 ather your friends\, and join Sonoma Valley Pride for one unforgettable ni
 ght at the Sebastiani Theatre.\n\nSF's Bawdy Caste\n\nThe Bawdy Caste is S
 an Francisco’s legendary Rocky Horror shadow cast\, bringing glitter\, f
 ishnets\, irreverence\, and unapologetic camp to stages across the Bay Are
 a and beyond for three decades.\n\nMore than a performance troupe\, The Ba
 wdy Caste celebrates individuality\, acceptance\, and community. Their sta
 ge is a space where people can be loud\, strange\, expressive\, and fully 
 themselves — creating an inclusive environment where everyone is encoura
 ged to feel seen\, welcomed\, and part of the fun.
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theatre
URL:https://sonomavalleypride.com/events/rocky-horror-picture-show-at-seba
 stiani-theater-50th-anniversary-screening-and-costume-contest/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
