BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Freestyle Playground Dance Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T193000
UID:261008edTeuAxFCU6JkfxJxWgqvQ
DESCRIPTION:Freestyle Playground — 4-Week Dance & Movement Series\n\n**E
 xplore. Play. Create. Express.**\n\nReady to discover new ways of moving a
 nd expressing yourself through dance?\n\n**Freestyle Playground** is a pla
 yful\, creative dance class designed to expand your movement vocabulary\, 
 spark your imagination\, and help you discover your own unique movement st
 yle.\n\nThrough guided freestyle exercises\, imaginative movement concepts
 \, musicality\, elements of popping\, rhythm\, and body awareness\, you'll
  explore new ways to move\, experiment\, and create.\n\nEach week\, we'll 
 introduce different movement tools and concepts that you can combine\, bui
 ld upon\, and incorporate into your own dancing.\n\n**This isn't a choreog
 raphy-based class.** It's about exploration\, curiosity\, and the freedom 
 to move without worrying about getting it "right."\n\nWhether you're an ex
 perienced dancer looking for fresh inspiration or someone curious about ex
 ploring movement\, all levels are welcome!\n\nClass Details\n\n📍 **Lagu
 na Lab | Sebastopol\, CA**\n\n📅 **4 Tuesdays: October 27\, November 3\,
  10 & 17**\n\n⏰ **6:30–7:30 PM**\n\n💃 **All levels welcome!**\n\nCo
 me expand your creativity\, discover new movement possibilities\, and expe
 rience the joy of freestyle dance!\n\n**No perfection. Just movement\, mus
 ic\, imagination & PLAY!**
LOCATION:Laguna Lab
URL:https://www.tickettailor.com/events/lagunalab/2417443
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T170000
UID:261004GXdSGv1nAku11WjSHJEGZg
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Kabbalah of Meaning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T193000
UID:2610013j_JVfbaPEqtPp5E4gPkag
DESCRIPTION:Jewish Wisdom for a Life That Matters\n\nNo matter how much we
  achieve\, something within us still asks: “Is this it? Isn’t there so
 mething more?”\n\nThe Kabbalah of Meaning is a new six-session JLI cours
 e exploring the Jewish answer to that question. What are we really searchi
 ng for—and where can it be found?\n\nDrawing on Kabbalah and centuries o
 f Jewish wisdom\, we’ll uncover the essential building blocks of a deepl
 y meaningful life. We’ll explore how purpose can be found in our work\, 
 relationships\, challenges\, accomplishments\, and even the ordinary routi
 nes that fill our days.\n\nYou don’t have to revamp your life. You don
 ’t need to meditate on a mountaintop. You simply need a new lens through
  which to see the rich world of meaning already woven into every part of y
 our life.\n\nThoughtful\, practical\, and surprisingly relevant\, this cou
 rse offers fresh perspectives and useful tools for living with greater cla
 rity\, connection\, and intention.\n\nTry 1st class free.\n\nNo previous J
 ewish learning required. Come as you are—and bring your questions.
LOCATION:Chabad Jewish Center of Petaluma
URL:https://www.jewishpetaluma.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/7522546/je
 wish/The-Kabbalah-of-Meaning.htm
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T170000
UID:260930bvvxqlo25kCkJU2FOGxmuw
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two *ofrendas* in the House of Happy Walls Museum from 
 Oct. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tra
 dition that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spa
 nish for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the mem
 ory of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and ad
 venturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected t
 o the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, tradi
 tional elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, 
 the installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing an
 d travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, an
 d the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared
 \, participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\
 , and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\
 , drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a 
 beloved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more pe
 ople participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitor
 s who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or
  even a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Independent Projects with Amy Hamley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T210000
UID:260926qpH_AsK7U0SFZFIQFqQ_oQ
DESCRIPTION:Every Tuesday · 6 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nOctober 6 – Novem
 ber 10th\, 2026\n\n6:00 PM – 9:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics 
 Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nI
 ntermediate\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Fee:\n\n$200\n\nMaterials Fee
 :\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$230\n\nThis is a 6 week session w
 ith instructor\, Amy Hamley. This course is for students interested in exp
 loring both wheel throwing AND handbuilding\, and the combination of both 
 in one class! Learn from Hamley’s years of expertise in the field and en
 joy creating handbuilt\, thrown\, and altered forms. Amy caters each sylla
 bus closely to her group of students\, ensuring that every project fits th
 e desires of participants. This course encourages folks to work on indepen
 dent projects in the class\, receiving one on one support from Amy through
 out the time. This course will include demos\, exercises\, and utilize a v
 ariety of methods to achieve the desired goal for each student. Some proje
 cts may include wheel thrown vases with altered adornments\, best practice
 s for slump and hump molds\, and more.
