BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bottega Cellar Series with Marchesi Antinori
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T210000
UID:261006sRgZrM3iRUOwOm1hMlbwXA
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Bottega on November 4th for an elegant evening feat
 uring Marchesi Antinori\, hosted by Estate Manager Glenn Salva. Marchesi A
 ntinori is a historic Tuscan winemaking family that helped pioneer the Sup
 er Tuscan movement. With a winemaking legacy dating back to 1385 and conti
 nuous family ownership\, the business is now led by the 26th generation wh
 o continue to guide Marchesi Antinori's tradition of bold innovation balan
 ced with deep respect for heritage and the land. The dinner will feature a
  selection of wines from the Antinori portfolio\, including Tignanello and
  Guado al Tasso. Guests will experience a thoughtfully curated progression
  of wines from one of Italy’s most storied wine families\, paired with a
  seasonal multi-course menu by Bottega Executive Chef Alex Espinoza. Each 
 course is designed to complement the character and expression of the wines
 \, bringing together refined flavors\, exceptional ingredients\, and the g
 racious hospitality that defines Bottega. Price is inclusive of tax and gr
 atuity.\n\n6525 Washington Street Suite A9\, Yountville\, CA 94599\n\n\\(7
 07\\) 945-1050
LOCATION:Bottega Napa Valley
URL:https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=25489&r
 estref=25489&experienceId=791062&utm_source=external&utm_medium=referral&u
 tm_campaign=shared
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
